{
  "table_id": "Table_S11",
  "display_number": "S11",
  "title": "Supplementary Table S11. Instrumental-variable validity diagnostics",
  "panel": "",
  "panel_title": "",
  "notes_before": [],
  "notes_after": [
    "Note. Instrument strength was assessed using cluster-robust first-stage F statistics in single-exposure models and Sanderson–Windmeijer conditional F statistics in dual-exposure models. F statistics greater than 10 were interpreted as evidence against weak instruments. Endogeneity was assessed using control-function (robust Durbin–Wu–Hausman) tests with participant-clustered standard errors; endogeneity of EVI was not detected in dual-exposure models (P = 0.103 and 0.109), whereas joint tests remained significant (P < 0.001). All models were exactly identified, so overidentification tests were not applicable.",
    "Abbreviations: EVI, enhanced vegetation index; ID, identification; IV, instrumental variable; O₃, ozone."
  ],
